Looking at the comment, I need to express: if the index range is valid, every bit in `[fromIndex, toIndex)` equals `value` after the operation.

The valid range condition (from the `@throws`): `fromIndex >= 0 && toIndex >= 0 && fromIndex <= toIndex`. The observer is `get(int bitIndex)` which returns the bit's value.

<code>assert (fromIndex >= 0 && toIndex >= 0 && fromIndex <= toIndex) => \forall int i; fromIndex <= i && i < toIndex; this.get(i) == value;</code>
